From: ROCKNIX/DUCKTALE
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: ayn-odin3: disable DP altmode (VBUS-in-suspend wedge)

The 7.1 bump brought the SM8750 display graph and with it USB-C
DisplayPort altmode (mdss_dp0 wired to the QMP combo phy, enabled in the
AYN dt). Since then, ANY charger plug/unplug while the device sits in
deep suspend wedges the SoC hard (forced reset only): the cable event
propagates through pmic_glink altmode -> typec mode-switch -> the DP
controller whose MDSS GDSC/dispcc domain is still gated during early
resume, and the register access hangs the NoC (no kernel crumbs
possible - DPM-watchdog/SDAM instrumentation stays empty).

7.0.11 with identical firmware had no mdss_dp0 node at all and never
wedged. Disable the DP controller until the altmode resume ordering is
fixed properly; USB-C video-out is lost, USB3 data is unaffected.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-common.dtsi
@@ -905,7 +905,12 @@
 };
 
 &mdss_dp0 {
-	status = "okay";
+	/*
+	 * DP altmode: a cable event in deep suspend reaches the DP
+	 * controller before its power domain resumes -> NoC hang.
+	 * Keep disabled until the resume ordering is fixed.
+	 */
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &mdss_dsi0 {
